<title>JAPAN: Japan MOF says to act if forex move excessive - Jiji.</title>
<headline>Japan MOF says to act if forex move excessive - Jiji.</headline>
<dateline>TOKYO 1997-04-10</dateline>
<text>
<p>Finance Minister Hiroshi Mitsuzuka was quoted as saying by Jiji news agency on Thursday that Japan will act appropriately if currency movements are excessive.  </p>
<p>&quot;As I have said before, our basic policy is that we will act appropriately when moves are excessive,&quot; Mitsuzuka was quoted as telling reporters by Japan's Jiji news agency.</p>
<p>He was also quoted as saying that a business tie-up between Japan's Nippon Credit Bank (NCB) and Bankers Trust New York Corp would help secure the implementation of NCB's restructuring plans.</p>
</text>
